  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat overtime multiplier applies to Mark's weekend work? Mark used to make $11 per hour.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. Overtime is commonly paid at **time-and-a-half**.\n2. “Time-and-a-half” means a multiplier of  \n   \\[\n   1+\\frac{1}{2}=1.5.\n   \\]\n3. Mark’s former wage of \\$11 per hour does not change the multiplier. (If used, the overtime rate would be \\(11 \\times 1.5=\\$16.50\\) per hour.)\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1.5\\times}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Mark used to make $10 per hour.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "1. Overtime is paid at **time-and-a-half**, regardless of whether Mark earned \\$10 or \\$11 per hour.\n2. The multiplier is therefore:\n   \\[\n   1+\\frac{1}{2}=1.5.\n   \\]\n3. At \\$10 per hour, his overtime wage would be:\n   \\[\n   \\$10 \\times 1.5=\\$15 \\text{ per hour}.\n   \\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1.5\\times}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How much would Mark earn for an 8-hour regular workday? Additionally, Mark works 8 regular hours in a standard weekday shift.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark’s regular hourly wage is \\$10, and he works 8 regular hours:\n\n\\[\n8 \\times \\$10 = \\$80\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$80}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Mark works 8 hours a day for 6 days a week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark works:\n\n\\[\n8 \\text{ hours/day} \\times 6 \\text{ days/week}=48 \\text{ hours/week}.\n\\]\n\nAssuming overtime applies after 40 hours per week:\n\n- Regular hours: \\(40 \\times \\$10=\\$400\\)\n- Overtime hours: \\(48-40=8\\)\n- Overtime rate: \\(\\$10 \\times 1.5=\\$15\\)\n- Overtime pay: \\(8 \\times \\$15=\\$120\\)\n\nTherefore, Mark earns:\n\n\\[\n\\$400+\\$120=\\boxed{\\$520\\text{ per week}}\n\\]\n\nThe 8-hour regular workday itself still earns \\(\\boxed{\\$80}\\).",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How much money does Mark make in one week? One more thing you should know: Mark's pay was raised by $2 per hour.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark’s new regular wage is:\n\n\\[\n\\$10+\\$2=\\$12\\text{ per hour}\n\\]\n\nHe works \\(48\\) hours per week:\n\n- Regular pay: \\(40 \\times \\$12=\\$480\\)\n- Overtime rate: \\(1.5 \\times \\$12=\\$18\\) per hour\n- Overtime pay: \\(8 \\times \\$18=\\$144\\)\n\nTotal weekly earnings:\n\n\\[\n\\$480+\\$144=\\boxed{\\$624}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Mark's employer pays 1.5 times the regular hourly rate for weekend work.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark’s raised regular wage is:\n\n\\[\n\\$10+\\$2=\\$12\\text{ per hour}\n\\]\n\nHe works 8 hours for each of 6 days, including one weekend day:\n\n- **40 weekday hours:**  \n  \\[\n  40 \\times \\$12=\\$480\n  \\]\n- **8 weekend hours at 1.5×:**  \n  \\[\n  8 \\times (1.5\\times \\$12)=8\\times \\$18=\\$144\n  \\]\n\nThus, Mark earns:\n\n\\[\n\\$480+\\$144=\\boxed{\\$624\\text{ per week}}\n\\]\n\nThis assumes the weekend premium is not stacked on top of overtime; both rates are 1.5×, so the result remains the same.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Mark works 8 hours a day for 5 days a week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Mark’s new regular rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\$10+\\$2=\\$12\\text{ per hour}\n\\]\n\nHe works:\n\n\\[\n8\\times 5=40\\text{ hours per week}\n\\]\n\nAssuming **one of those five shifts is on the weekend**:\n\n- 4 regular weekday shifts:\n  \\[\n  4\\times 8\\times \\$12=\\$384\n  \\]\n- 1 weekend shift at \\(1.5\\) times the regular rate:\n  \\[\n  8\\times(1.5\\times \\$12)=8\\times\\$18=\\$144\n  \\]\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[\n\\$384+\\$144=\\boxed{\\$528\\text{ per week}}\n\\]\n\nIf all five shifts are weekdays, he would earn \\(\\$480\\) per week.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
